    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So you're saying the \"intellectual complexity\" is basically tied to how much they follow Western academic standards? If a non-Western artist were to master perspective and chiaroscuro, would their work then be considered just as \"sophisticated\" as the Renaissance piece, or is there still something about the nature of \"folk\" or \"tribal\" art that keeps it in a different category regardless of technical skill?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
